{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact R15 head 5919361a43448631f29102c5a480387979d8dcdd on builder/hosted-retirement-r15-20261109, tree d3fc9689, all 20 artifacts, for request b66b8f14 under promise 0875dbf1 and review request ade51757. Retire now disables the hosted endpoint and erases its signing seed in one SQLite transaction. It completes only when membership records the key's revocation. The repair after the failed gate meets the isolated-test rule in docs/testing.md.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- Shutdown. `#retire` runs after the existing `bound`, membership and `authorityOf` checks, on the same `#controls` queue as create, bearer and grant. One transaction sets `state = 'retired'`, writes an empty seed, clears the bearer, ends OAuth access, deletes both session tables, refunds their budget and records the control row as pending. Only after that commit does it zero the in-memory seed, close transports, revoke issuer grants and read or dispatch anything outside. The constructor also empties the seed of any row already retired.\n- Cached service ports. The service signer and `fetch` reread the row on every call. They act only while `op` and `key` are unchanged, the state is `enrolling` or `enrolled`, and the seed holds 32 bytes. Signing copies the seed and zeroes the copy. A retained intent prepared before retirement therefore cannot sign or dispatch afterwards.\n- No revival. `#create` returns 409 on a retired row before it builds or signs anything, and its final transaction refuses a retired row again. Bearer on a retired row still answers 409.\n- The caller's revoke. `retirementBody` accepts an empty body, `{}` or exactly `{revoke}`. A revoke must verify, be signed by the control's actor, address this membership, be `revoke-key` with one field, `as: \"retired\"`, and name an item of at least 1. `enrolledKeyItem` takes the target only from this endpoint's accepted, verified enrol envelope for the same identity, and returns null otherwise. The endpoint submits the envelope only when its `on` equals that item and its `notAfter` has not passed. The first envelope is stored once (`revoke IS NULL` guard). A later body cannot replace it, and the agent's seed never signs a revoke. Native membership still judges the signer's authority.\n- Completion. `200` requires an observed `retired` or `compromised` key standing. Every other path answers `202` with the endpoint disabled, the seed erased and a named reason. A retry re-observes and can complete after any admin or recovery revoke.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 6dd337d3 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 20 paths that its 20 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 12 checked, 0 flagged. No dependency, lockfile, Wrangler, definition, pin, creation family or migration file changes. The new `agent_retirement` table starts empty.\n- The seals. I recomputed both outside the builder's worktree. hosted.ts gives c41049c9… and hosted-retirement.ts gives 8707c99f…, each equal to its literal. Each sealed change is the one described above. No route check, authority check or check order moves.\n- The failed gate stays failed. Gate 522949c7 read `exit 1` at typecheck. Every earlier step passed. The log holds exactly two errors, both in hosted.scope.test.ts at lines 1899 and 1915, where the test's RPC seed value is typed `string | Uint8Array`.\n- The isolated-test rule. Between 522949c7 and f34e58db only hosted.scope.test.ts changes, by six lines: the seed now crosses the RPC as a number array and becomes the same `Uint8Array`. The note and the failed-gate manifest are the only other changes. No other file imports that test. The one other mention, in apps/room/page/test/mcp-original.scope.test.ts, is a comment. No case, assertion or deadline changes. Production, helpers, configuration and dependencies equal the gate's. The follow-up ran the failed MCP Worker context, the MCP browser context, all ten root contexts, the complete `npm test` body and the summary. I read each of the 16 exit files as `exit 0`. After f34e58db, only the note and two manifests change.\n- The control. At ffc97d5d, omitting only the seed assignment and its binding fails the two new cases at lines 1882 and 1938, with 0 bytes expected and 32 found. The other 22 cases pass. The original verifier exited 1 because Vitest abbreviated the first message. The reconciliation over the same run's full stderr exits 0 and keeps the verifier's failure on record. The source is restored.\n- The evidence. The five manifests that I read hash to the cited values. Their 137 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The note keeps the six failed focused units and the failed gate as failures.\n- Docs. docs/mcp.md describes 200 and 202, the retained envelope, recovery and the existing 300-second grant lifetime. The entry-point inventory adds hosted-retirement.ts.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The two pure helpers decide the body and the target. `#retire` owns the order: commit the shutdown, then do outside work. The membership rules and their meaning do not change. Kernel section 7: the change adds no kernel item. It is a filed R1–R16 security fix in the hosted MCP service, so section 7.1's exception covers it.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A retired endpoint cannot sign, dispatch, mint a bearer or finish an enrollment. It cannot relay any act other than one revoke of its own key item, signed by the retiring party. One limit holds by design, and docs/mcp.md states it: a grant that another scope already holds lasts up to 300 seconds after retirement.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: a malformed retire body answers 400 before shutdown, so it leaves the endpoint enabled. That keeps the signed body's meaning exact. A caller who wants shutdown alone sends an empty body.\n\nThe planner deploys after landing. No setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b555e5d16fcc7657b8d2dcb06214599eddb1f60","binding":"assigned","head":"5919361a43448631f29102c5a480387979d8dcdd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d998e40c6dc8c31e314b295fb0f23d2e12305d0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0875dbf1182ef1ce98fa6119a6c2de06e3a2383b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d998e40c6dc8c31e314b295fb0f23d2e12305d0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}